    "created_at": "2022-03-14T20:53:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-14T20:53:00Z",
    "body": "Looking back at the [intent to ship](https://groups.google.com/g/mozilla.dev.platform/c/MSzaY7_4mvg/m/hGpUlTzxAgAJ) I think the main motivation for limiting this to secure origins was [Mozilla's policy](https://blog.mozilla.org/security/2018/01/15/secure-contexts-everywhere/) of doing so.\r\n\r\nI also seem to recall a discussion where trailers were causing problems with middleboxes over HTTP, but I can't find any references to that at this time.",
