    "body": "> Looking back at the [intent to ship](https://groups.google.com/g/mozilla.dev.platform/c/MSzaY7_4mvg/m/hGpUlTzxAgAJ) I think the main motivation for limiting this to secure origins was [Mozilla's policy](https://blog.mozilla.org/security/2018/01/15/secure-contexts-everywhere/) of doing so.\r\n> \r\n> I also seem to recall a discussion where trailers were causing problems with middleboxes over HTTP, but I can't find any references to that at this time.\r\n\r\nSeems like the conversation [didn't result in a consensus](https://github.com/w3c/server-timing/issues/54), which is unfortunate since currently server-timing is not interoperable in that way. ",
